{"term":"nightmare","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:be532bcd50feb322c2","definition":"A very unpleasant or frightening dream.","example":"I had a nightmare that I tried to run but could neither move nor breathe.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["daymare","flightmare","frightmare","knightmare","logistical nightmare","mid-nightmare","midnightmare","morningmare","nightmare disorder","nightmare fuel","nightmareless","nightmarelike","nightmarious","nightmarish","nightmary","out of a nightmare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightmare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c6dc3fb8fe8851bd77","definition":"Any bad, miserable, difficult or terrifying situation or experience that arouses anxiety, terror, agony or great displeasure.","example":"Cleaning up after identity theft can be a nightmare of phone calls and letters.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["incubus","succubus","night hag"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["daymare","flightmare","frightmare","knightmare","logistical nightmare","mid-nightmare","midnightmare","morningmare","nightmare disorder","nightmare fuel","nightmareless","nightmarelike","nightmarious","nightmarish","nightmary","out of a nightmare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightmare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:acf23b4b4b4edebfb8","definition":"A demon or monster, thought to plague people while they slept and cause a feeling of suffocation and terror during sleep.","example":"It haunted me, however, more than once, like a night-mare.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["daymare","flightmare","frightmare","knightmare","logistical nightmare","mid-nightmare","midnightmare","morningmare","nightmare disorder","nightmare fuel","nightmareless","nightmarelike","nightmarious","nightmarish","nightmary","out of a nightmare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightmare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ebef1495ef0a53f79b","definition":"A feeling of extreme anxiety or suffocation experienced during sleep; sleep paralysis.","example":"The Night-mare generally ſeizes people ſleeping on their backs, and often begins with frightful dreams, which are ſoon ſucceeded by a difficult reſpiration, a violent oppreſſion on the breaſt, and a total privation of voluntary motion.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"historical","wordFamily":["daymare","flightmare","frightmare","knightmare","logistical nightmare","mid-nightmare","midnightmare","morningmare","nightmare disorder","nightmare fuel","nightmareless","nightmarelike","nightmarious","nightmarish","nightmary","out of a nightmare"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightmare#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:630a649722aafe331f","definition":"To experience a nightmare.","example":"Brother Fary of Omaha was nightmaring the rest of the night.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["daymare","flightmare","frightmare","knightmare","logistical nightmare","mid-nightmare","midnightmare","morningmare","nightmare disorder","nightmare fuel","nightmareless","nightmarelike","nightmarious","nightmarish","nightmary","out of a nightmare","night terror","sleep paralysis"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightmare#Eng